course: dictionary
lesson: 3529
title: Fearfully: two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Fearfully has two, so check the clues around it to see which one fits. «She looked fearfully at the dark door.» The clue is that she is scared, so fearfully means in a frightened or worried way.
explain: In old-fashioned British talk, fearfully can mean very or extremely. «He was fearfully clever at maths» does not mean he was scared of maths. It means he was extremely clever, because nobody is frightened when they are clever.
explain: The example «I praise you because I am fearfully and wonderfully made» uses the old sense. It means I am amazingly well made. Being honest about yourself includes your good bits too.
explain: To choose the right meaning, swap in a simple word and read the sentence again. If «scared» fits, use the frightened meaning. If «very» fits better, use the very meaning.
fact: Fearfully means in a frightened or worried way.
fact: In old-fashioned British talk, fearfully can mean very or extremely.
fact: Phrases to spot: «look fearfully» and «whisper fearfully» usually show fear; «fearfully sorry» means very sorry.
fact: A good check is to swap in another word: «scared» or «worried» for the fear meaning, or «very» for the old meaning.
fact: Same word, two meanings: the sentence around it tells you which one the writer means.
exercise: «She looked fearfully at the dark door.» What does fearfully mean here? | *In a frightened way | Very quickly | Happily, with a big smile | Very loudly
exercise: «He was fearfully clever at maths.» What does fearfully mean here? | In a frightened way | *Very, or extremely | Sadly | Slowly and carefully
exercise: «He whispered fearfully, "Is anyone there?"» What does whispered fearfully suggest? | A silly joke | *A worried, scared voice | A happy, bouncy voice | A loud shout
test: «I was fearfully sorry for breaking the vase.» What does fearfully mean here? | Scared of the vase | Not sorry at all | Quietly sorry, in a whisper | *Very sorry
test: Which word in «The cat crept fearfully past the dog» tells how the cat moved? | past | dog | cat | *fearfully
exam: Ruby reads «fearfully fast» in a book and says fearfully means scared. What is the best reply? | Ruby is right, it means scared | *Not quite: here it can mean very, so it means very fast | It means happy and bouncy | It means slowly and carefully
